From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Charlie <5764343+charlielye@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:15:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] refactor: read the canonical genesis from
 @aztec-foundation/protocol-genesis

The protocol release now ships its canonical genesis as data: the world state inputs, the protocol contracts'
registration nullifiers among them, and the nullifier tree root, genesis block header hash and archive root they
produce. Labs reads it instead of deriving it:

- DEFAULT_GENESIS_DATA and ProtocolContractGenesisNullifiers come from the package, and generate_data.ts no longer
  computes the nullifiers, so stdlib's computeProtocolGenesisNullifiers goes.
- @aztec-labs/constants re-exports GENESIS_BLOCK_HEADER_HASH, GENESIS_NULLIFIER_TREE_ROOT and GENESIS_ARCHIVE_ROOT
  from the package, since they are no longer protocol constants.
- genesis_data.test.ts compared the generated nullifiers with a TS recomputation; the foundation's genesis check
  now covers the package against the artifacts.
- compute-genesis-values no longer prints the canonical block, which only the old regeneration script read.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015HXzMEGRnmFYs5yXRcAWCb

